From: Bellatrix Project <bellatrix@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] vc4gfx: retarget the boot UI after FBALLOC

The Emu68 boot UI starts on the firmware's RGB565 surface.  vc4gfx later
asks the firmware for a BGRX8888 framebuffer, so continuing to draw through
the old geometry and pixel format briefly duplicates and splits the splash.

Hand the newly allocated surface to the port's boot UI before HVS takeover.
This keeps the early display coherent across the framebuffer mode change.

---
 .../2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c         | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c
index 550a54de3a..92549b58f1 100644
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <proto/mbox.h>
 #ifdef __EMU68__
 #include <aros/kernel.h>
+#include <aros/bootui.h>
 #include <proto/kernel.h>
 #endif
 #include <proto/utility.h>
@@ -332,6 +333,11 @@ static BOOL vc4_program_fb(struct VideoCoreGfx_staticdata *xsd,
     }
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __EMU68__
+    emu68_bootui_retarget(fb_ptr, fb_pitch, aligned_width, height,
+                          bitsperpixel);
+#endif
+
     /* Phase-1 HVS bring-up: dump the firmware's live display list and PV
      * timing for this mode (read-only, self-skips on QEMU). */
     vc4_hvs_dump(xsd, (ULONG)(IPTR)fb_ptr, fb_pitch, aligned_width, height);
-- 
